      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no \"logical change\", it\u0027s like a copy/paste of what was here. The main difference is that it no longer exposes the service; it now uses the \"Rust FFI\", which is a mirror of the AIDL interface (https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/3407740/16/offload/hal/ffi.h).\n\nIt looks like there are significant changes, because of formatting, but definitely there is not. Just move to the interface:\n```\nextern \"C\" {\n\nusing namespace aidl::android::hardware::bluetooth::impl;\n\nstruct hal_interface hal_new() {\n  return (struct hal_interface){\n      .handle \u003d new Hal(),\n      .initialize \u003d \u0026Hal::Initialize,\n      .close \u003d \u0026Hal::Close,\n      .send_command \u003d \u0026Hal::SendCommand,\n      .send_acl \u003d \u0026Hal::SendAcl,\n      .send_sco \u003d \u0026Hal::SendSco,\n      .send_iso \u003d \u0026Hal::SendIso,\n  };\n}\n}\n```\n\nFrom my understanding of this code, it\u0027s just enabled on \"Cuttefish\", henrichataing@google.com is currently working on Cuttlefish port in Rust.\n\nI kept this with an FFI, as vendors are not ready to move to Rust; it\u0027s to simplify the integration\u0027s work (fallback to C).\n\nAbout fuzzing, I don\u0027t know how easily porting it, as the C++ binder interface is no more used. But from my understanding, it was not enabled, or has been disabled, I don\u0027t know. If disabled, there is probably reason for that...\nFor this reason, I didn\u0027t feel like I changed anything.\nIt\u0027s not a refactor / cleanup but integration of the HCI part of LE Audio Software offload.\n\nI can work on reenabling it on the \"C part\", but I think it should be part of another CL.\n\nWhat do you think?",
